    "notes": "Bout set and back length are the Library of Congress catalogue dimensions, verbatim: length of back 410.6 mm, upper bouts 183 mm, middle bouts 123 mm, lower bouts 237 mm. Everything in params below the catalogue dimensions is unsolved and carries DefaultParams values - the outline arcs, corners, button and blocks are still to be traced. No arching: none is published. Licence differs from the CC0 corpus entries: the LoC record carries its educational-and-research rights statement rather than a public-domain dedication, so the images are linked at their IIIF addresses rather than inlined. Four views are shipped from the record: the top (sp=2) as the general view, marked Default, kept off the panels that have their own; the top and back (sp=1) side by side on fluting; and the profile plate (sp=3), which photographs both sides of the instrument, cropped to its left-hand half for longArching. crossArching is excluded outright - no section is published, and that panel shows nothing rather than a plan shot that would be traced by mistake. The rest of the record is corner, edge, rib, scroll and pegbox detail; where a set holds an annotated measured drawing it is a third party's own analysis, deliberately not shipped and not to be traced from. Reference images are placed to a nominal fit only - plan views at the catalogue lower-bout width, the profile at the catalogue back length, each held to its source proportions - so every one must be scaled against a known dimension before tracing."
